# NEPSE cost-basis side file — one row per holding.
#
# MeroShare doesn't export cost basis; you maintain it here by hand.
# scripts/normalize_meroshare_csv.py joins this file with the raw
# MeroShare export to produce data/nepse_portfolio.csv in the tracker
# schema (symbol, shares, avg_cost, entry_date, is_margin).
#
# Where to find cost basis:
#   - IPO / bonus allotments: cost = par value (typically NPR 100)
#   - Market buys: check your broker's TMS → Transaction History
#   - Inherited / gifted shares: book value at transfer date
#
# Copy this file to data/cost_basis.csv and edit. Lines starting with #
# are ignored. Add one row per NEPSE symbol you hold.
symbol,avg_cost,entry_date,is_margin
NABIL,1180.00,2025-12-15,false
UPPER,425.00,2026-03-22,true
NICA,890.00,2026-04-10,false
